  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_be2b165aa3f449298142345d4d7de3fc",
      "statement": "The engine has no per-type code: a document primitive's required_fields, optional_fields, immutable_fields, required_when, enums, patterns, references, append_only flag, portability class, and resource.binds metadata all come from registry/core.json and extension registries, resolved at runtime by src/registry.mjs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://registry/core.json#L8-L250",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ac7eaae9838d670be13723f134db1792ab136a8af3f98272a5d40da98c99b946:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/registry.mjs#L1-L10",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b146a11bf0770daae7ddabe0067d995046f45852b18845485fd4158cf4794fda:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_32a01c86278346bc86304aa4251f550b",
      "statement": "composeRegistries composes the package core with extension registry objects: it validates each primitive definition, resolves bare and qualified aliases bidirectionally, rejects core/extension and cross-extension name collisions as hard errors (§5.6), enforces extension namespace prefixes, semver-checks extension requires, and verifies that every reference allowed_types/disallowed_types names a known primitive with no allow/forbid overlap through aliases.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/registry.mjs#L149-L281",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7d86a4a5591909b24d4ea64f653750a694d02221e0331848190b043b55964b4b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e48c540b58374017bbd548d780b1ff40",
      "statement": "loadRegistries reads core.json plus a non-symlinked extensions/ directory, using the package core when an application registry dir holds only extensions, and scopes loading via extensions/defaults.json or an explicit options.only set so unrelated product extensions that share a primitive name do not collide.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/registry.mjs#L389-L450",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:58d3df06acbafa65f295b335062f30d734355937f54b04c428000ad97da63da9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_83346ed17fcb437ca1df073d34ba3241",
      "statement": "resolvePortability computes a file's effective portability class as the most restrictive of the type default and an x_portability frontmatter override, using the order structural (0) -> resource_bound (1) -> tenant_private (2); an override can only escalate restrictiveness, never relax it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/registry.mjs#L459-L469",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bc1fcb9e85efbe5f83f39912cc5bd4edb58137366035c98bbf7abf777e586ca1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_eaad15bea91c403ab00f74dadfa28afc",
      "statement": "The three portability classes are structural (sellable business model), tenant_private (operator private data, never sold/templated, only encrypted backup), and resource_bound (needs a real external resource bound at provision time); contract primitives carry no portability class.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://registry/core.json#L267-L281",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:373784318c15e2ed6b5a29510a7d56fb35372e241176f17f385edf223e745ea8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_da98dc2a07a64020a215a0c15c72c438",
      "statement": "The three export profiles are filters over the portability classes: backup includes all three (tenant_private encrypted at rest), while template and sale include structural + resource_bound and exclude tenant_private; template/sale must drop every tenant_private primitive and reduce every resource_bound primitive to a requirement declaration.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://registry/core.json#L274-L279",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:114493f2d48afdf28dff92eda616717daae2c0961db4826fb915a74f2a2e9917:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bundle.mjs#L30-L34",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6d7e6214b2990c63e1338a7038ef1d722110a48954b189025514bc2c190ad093:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_81a0cae2364049aa8c71d5a54c5b012e",
      "statement": "During template/sale export, reduceResourceBoundFile sets x_portability to resource_bound and replaces every field named in the type's resource.binds with the literal REQUIREMENT; ensureRequirementDeclarations adds a user-source provisioning parameter and a provision-mode bind step per bound field; a resource_bound type with no resource.binds causes export to throw.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bundle.mjs#L189-L203",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cb22444d5c58a1a55811c28cbd5ba5aa6f6bfadbf8300920921640f878eb6c34:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bundle.mjs#L71-L114",
